{"title":"2025 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Satisfying_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Satisfying and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Easy_to_identify)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Easy to identify)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Ratio)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Ratio)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:10)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:10)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Chinese_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Chinese Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Continuum Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c746b01f0187cd1a9ad159e12dcd85ff79dad95f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> is arithmetic. The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0ff4d235e1505649fed190cef1fa519c3e764b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,p,q,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> is geometric. Both sequences are strictly increasing and contain only integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is as small as possible. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d075dcd626c16d971314af547e9c079a6078ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z+p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655f9ff074a0f05d2cad6a5f0076a3b9a1a7917a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 66 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 91 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 103 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 132 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"428\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the geometric sequence is more restrictive, we can test values for the common ratio until we find one that works. After a few tests, we find that a common ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> results in the geometric sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/1653afd5eac249b3b2ea11d38895daff46c21314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,4,16,64,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> so the arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/8/f88c5b588da9f42cb0abe5053d0e1917ab8e7278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,22,43,64.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" /> The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bd74601b74d6313ee401927e1183dec2ab02b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+16+64+22+43=\\boxed{\\text{(E) }149}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"270\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>A more generalized solution is as follows. \nLet the common difference of the arithmetic sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the common ratio of the geometric sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279a83610a37e3f83bb8d2544695241ca8066834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> Hence, the two sequences are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5f0c546446b409f78958e9b816430410e4789e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,1+d,1+2d,1+3d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e9405f9a3950a6e745f0685d9ca3b1f3f5965d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,r,r^2,r^3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee4b4e51fea3561592f85e1d87ca96b6ab77bb52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1+3d=r^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> the arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/2040ae0e58cd6f76c133583c0c6d081d80275e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,1+d,1+2d,r^3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a9382511799207bfddc5aa4bba68ba4190069881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\dfrac{1+3d-1}{3}=\\dfrac{r^3-1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"196\" height=\"41\" /> is a positive integer, we seek the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5edcc8f911db56af92e4bd91f78fcf7e8b809ecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/1/3c1dd34331cb0fffb4292235954c5110f5e69946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3-1=(r-1)(r^2+r+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"21\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> so the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The rest follows like above.\n</p><p>~Tacos_are_yummy_1\n</p><p>~Minor edit by dodobird150\n</p><p>~Minor spelling fix by Eggplant123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c502366113ff4471622c928bc8b942ef23ca27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> is an arithmetic sequence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed3aab0588b79b17b1b89c37709a62db376b52b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8344d51af9b9d4e458697415c4e83583691b01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 3x - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/194cae43897dd26324b9d57a5d5e205ccd6c0ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, p, q, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> is a geometric sequence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50eef0a7ee929166c7c292ef1d101482e629c8ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1de82c63bf32f4be59ad49737672ee10bb2e1a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = p^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />.\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0cd0a67cd74372f13282e9f2509d3eb7f671f5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^3 = 3x - 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca27a4e9f7df010f5c6141ae8057b079a018c70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^3 \\equiv p \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551f53510d3deb24cd7cb5b5cbf73a861ac36426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x - 2 \\equiv p \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/556c2d1c580b3c7c46a19a6437efd8c47b3305ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />.\nThe smallest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc86688cd9e5a4ce262df69345bacac9f89f8ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> satisfying this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be241415c542a527773b9c883ce3cba4c07f1d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beac9290152eccf1f4bd052dc6c0b6f0bea6b348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 = 3x - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" /> → <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd67b74d4735ba01663051073d3bbe2dd78d4b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 22$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d8e79953fa3583bdc1b2ec4116c185349d0c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb98e06ef7665561ad60dfa0db6785701985727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/666efa8eff20efb239b94b2bbe1da007adbc0c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />.\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11a45d9e976afe128db55c9bfaf8e6bb8d40ef22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + z + p + q = 22 + 43 + 64 + 4 + 16 = \\boxed{\\text{(E) }149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"425\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Continuous_Pi\n</p><p>~<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> by stevens0209\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Satisfying_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Satisfying_and_Simple)\">Solution 3 (Satisfying and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Satisfying and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>So we have that the arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8063f8bb403ce3c1cf2912ce20849d76c4a46b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, x, 2x-1, 3x-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"17\" /> since\ncommon difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b0495af1d7b094561fcade343847d464778c925d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, geometric sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8c3e6e0c3c4fdbd553bc053b3812896e531243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, p, p^2, p^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c2a4c0c93bc514432c5d8c90e7cafd3ba707b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^3 = 3x-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />. We test values above 1 (increasing sequence)\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/3893d0ddadbf999b0cdf9e3a1188937f68a8c3dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 4, x = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db46a99737086c071a4945f7468db93783c4fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 + 43 + 64 + 4 + 16 = \\boxed{149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"235\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Aarav22\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Easy_to_identify.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Easy_to_identify)\">Solution 4 (Easy to identify)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Easy to identify)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since only integer ratios work for the geometric series, test the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, by having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cubed, and finding that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b4cc7f59163463b33bd527cecd7b8d137247b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64-1}{3}=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" /> (since that is the common ratio of the arithmetic sequence to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms), then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb458a5a27b6c1404d5574156d683175a609c496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22+43+4+16+64=149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"224\" height=\"15\" />, which is E.\n</p><p>Note: We divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because to get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> you have to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b26c8398882a95a9099c7b9516439dd6b467c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> which is the difference of the arithmetic sum.\n</p><p>-Amon26(note)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Ratio.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Ratio)\">Solution 5 (Ratio)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Ratio)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c502366113ff4471622c928bc8b942ef23ca27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> as an arithmetic sequence. If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the rate of change, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94b12e11ed0cad75ad7a903866f1c4f2f2eb1ec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z - y = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7b9f789967d350f93a2ec61ce504345225aa54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - x = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421430d94f85eec9e0aadcfb1f6cc3d58fc8c622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 1 = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, now you could follow with solution 3, or, you could just have the geometric sequence ratio be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5f08f485f55bdfe8423a03f7b4a1cf9f44a4c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{z}{q} = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/43607fd392a4e0a41edaa05f88923b6ab18203ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{q}{p} = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a896b13d5aed921064be839ecf0691c921ebb1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{1} = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Wait, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a896b13d5aed921064be839ecf0691c921ebb1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{1} = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"34\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e755b804241d49c2e53d386a6616a2a1d4ecf26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50eef0a7ee929166c7c292ef1d101482e629c8ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/2697831c98eab1ec73065dc22fa0487d02babba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^3 = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />, and since these have to be integers, we have to get a value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that works as an integer for the arithmetic sequence.\n</p><p>Because we add our common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> 3 times, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c319d077c2e0d88b16ab59734fb12892b4b02661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p^3-1)/3=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"21\" /> where d is an integer (this is because if we try 3 we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a450a368c84e87655a9aee9b7e8f1ecf3f5b8d4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> which violates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/2697831c98eab1ec73065dc22fa0487d02babba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^3 = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5bee8bc4dabea7532e7359aa8ac83217db2f4dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, however, the starting is one, so we find a value that when subtracted by 1, gets us a multiple of 3 so the arithmetic sequence works) and we find a value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be241415c542a527773b9c883ce3cba4c07f1d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48501757de81e300aabe29ddcda9279cf62e130f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 22, 43, 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d2e1f9f378caa80c2c7af7dd601d7c21e36c71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> and it follows as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b545017eefeecc70c939dab1aa4e38cc41ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^3 - 1 = 63 = 3d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />, and adding it up we get 129 for the arithmetic and since 64 is already <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> so we only need to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, we would get 20 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/001753b061f161c9611e32626db98f5ae244e9c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + 129 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>- Randomuser456\n(Note there are definitely other values where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c319d077c2e0d88b16ab59734fb12892b4b02661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p^3-1)/3=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"21\" /> is true, however the problem says for the lowest value of z) and this is also my first solution, please change things if necessary:)\n</p>\n<pre> ^_^\n /|\\  👍\n  |\n / \\\n</pre>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:10.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:10)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:10)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:10)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/AKmgcSIVTnQ\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/AKmgcSIVTnQ</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5Fjos1vBt0A\">https://youtu.be/5Fjos1vBt0A</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vuofaWEXiiQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vuofaWEXiiQ</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Chinese_Video_Solution\">Chinese Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Chinese Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1JYkUBVEMw/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1JYkUBVEMw/</a>\n</p><p>~metrixgo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math\">Video Solution by Continuum Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Continuum Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/yjSlq3oH2yI\">https://youtu.be/yjSlq3oH2yI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mxA52qodEqk?si=jxyGlehyqeHxic1i\">https://youtu.be/mxA52qodEqk?si=jxyGlehyqeHxic1i</a> ~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dAeyV60Hu5c</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gWSZeCKrOfU\">https://youtu.be/gWSZeCKrOfU</a>\n</p><p>~MK\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5TC6i3mEPXk\">https://youtu.be/5TC6i3mEPXk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class